<title>USA: Health Care REIT Q4 shr net rises to $0.55.</title>
<headline>Health Care REIT Q4 shr net rises to $0.55.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.55		    $0.06</p>
<p> Net			  9,046			786</p>
<p> Revs			14,818		   11,978</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  16,410		   11,835</p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.18		    $1.16</p>
<p> Net			 30,676		   13,635</p>
<p> Revs			54,402		   44,596</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,093		   11,710</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full name of company is Health Care REIT Inc.</p>
<p>Q4 funds from operations were $9.14 million in profit or $0.56 per share, compared to a loss of $175,000 or $0.01 per share for the same period in 1995. Full-year funds from operations were $30.3 million or $2.15 per share, compared to $11.1 million or $0.95 per share in 1995.</p>
<p>The company's 1995 results were hurt by one-time charges that exceeded $10 million.</p>
